WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.082
Three case studies show what happens when
RRI is missing, and what a responsible

2
00:00:05.082 --> 00:00:06.935
approach would have looked like.

3
00:00:08.135 --> 00:00:13.575
In the first case, an EU-funded firm
builds an AI system to streamline access to

4
00:00:13.575 --> 00:00:14.663
public services.

5
00:00:14.943 --> 00:00:19.234
At rollout, it disproportionately
misclassifies people from marginalised

6
00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:22.154
communities, who are then
excluded from services.

7
00:00:23.354 --> 00:00:29.009
There was no stakeholder consultation, no
participatory design, and no anticipation

8
00:00:29.009 --> 00:00:30.031
of social risk.

9
00:00:30.311 --> 00:00:35.000
Early impact assessment, participatory
design, and the AREA framework would have

10
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:35.410
helped.

11
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:41.187
In the second case, a national smart
meter programme aims to improve energy

12
00:00:41.187 --> 00:00:41.858
efficiency.

13
00:00:42.138 --> 00:00:45.829
But citizens object to surveillance
and data protection risks.

14
00:00:46.109 --> 00:00:48.157
They were never informed or involved.

15
00:00:48.437 --> 00:00:51.210
Trust collapses, and the
programme is suspended.

16
00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:57.512
Foresight exercises, public deliberation
before deployment, and privacy designed in

17
00:00:57.512 --> 00:01:00.709
from the start, could have
built legitimacy instead.

18
00:01:01.909 --> 00:01:07.194
In the third case, a university consortium
begins field trials of a geoengineering

19
00:01:07.194 --> 00:01:10.933
technology, with little
consultation of local communities.

20
00:01:11.213 --> 00:01:13.901
Protests and media
coverage pause the project.

21
00:01:15.101 --> 00:01:19.815
Engaging communities through co-design,
being transparent, and sharing benefits

22
00:01:19.815 --> 00:01:23.335
fairly, would have fostered
mutual understanding and trust.

23
00:01:24.535 --> 00:01:26.669
Different technologies, same pattern.

24
00:01:26.949 --> 00:01:31.621
In each case, anticipation, inclusion
and responsiveness came too late.

25
00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:36.466
When engagement comes late, trust is
lost, and projects stall or cause harm.

26
00:01:36.746 --> 00:01:39.413
Early, genuine engagement is not a delay.

27
00:01:39.693 --> 00:01:41.783
It is how research earns public trust.

28
00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:44.327
Thank you for watching.

29
00:01:44.607 --> 00:01:48.127
Continue with the module to
put these ideas into practice.
